[2026-09-07T17:08:19.561Z] [22e83702-0b77-461a-8405-d985649d221f] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=54 | rootCause=The render is not executing the intended 15s premium commercial edit cleanly. It starts strong, but then wastes time on repeated process beats, underuses the best hero platter, and the on-screen CTA appears over the wrong visual for too long. The biggest failure is that the reel feels like stacked raw footage with minimal editorial control rather than a finished Reel with a clear process-to-payoff arc. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"PACING","timestamp_seconds":2.5,"problem":"The cut lingers on the same rolling action for too many seconds, creating a dead middle with repeated visual information.","fix":"Compress the rolling beat to a short 1.0-1.4s insert and cut immediately into the premium detail/flame beat."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"CONTINUITY","timestamp_seconds":9.5,"problem":"A human reaction shot appears in the payoff section and feels unrelated to the sushi craft sequence, breaking the commercial flow.","fix":"Remove the reaction insert entirely and keep the reel product-only until the CTA."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"TYPOGRAPHY","timestamp_seconds":12.5,"problem":"The final CTA text sits over the chef prep shot for several frames instead of clearly landing on the hero platter, so the brand message is visually mismatched.","fix":"Move the CTA onto the top-down platter shot and keep the copy minimal: brand name plus 'Tonight' or 'Visit Tonight'."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"VISUAL_VARIETY","timestamp_seconds":4.5,"problem":"Multiple adjacent frames are nearly identical, especially in the rolling section, making the edit feel static despite fast pacing intent.","fix":"Replace duplicate holds with either a tighter crop change or a shorter cut duration."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"BRAND","timestamp_seconds":12.5,"problem":"Brand lock-up is present, but the composition does not feel like a deliberate final brand moment.","fix":"Reserve the cleanest hero platter as the full-end branding frame with generous negative space."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"AUDIO","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The render preview gives no clear evidence of a finished commercial audio mix; SFX and music impact are not perceptibly elevated in the visual result.","fix":"Ensure the hook has a distinct hit, the transition beats have subtle whooshes/impacts, and the CTA lands with a stronger audio sting."}]
