[2026-09-07T17:13:55.932Z] [22e83702-0b77-461a-8405-d985649d221f] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=2 | score=67 | rootCause=The render has a strong opening hook, but it collapses into repetition and weak story progression. The midsection overuses the same rolling/plating visual language, then the ending sits too long on a CTA overlay without enough payoff variety. The biggest issue is execution mismatch: the plan promises a finished commercial feel with dynamic audio/text/timing, but the rendered reel mostly reads as a string of similar food-process frames with no visible evidence of the intended editorial sophistication. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Pacing/Repetition","timestamp_seconds":3,"problem":"The reel stalls in the middle with nearly identical rolling/plating frames, creating dead time and weakening retention.","fix":"Collapse the repeated rolling shots into one short craft beat and move on quickly to a contrasting premium plating/hero shot."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Visual Variety","timestamp_seconds":10,"problem":"The portrait tasting/reaction section feels off-brand and visually detached from the culinary craft montage.","fix":"Remove the reaction insert entirely and replace it with a tighter food hero or clean platter hold from existing sushi footage."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Continuity","timestamp_seconds":5.5,"problem":"The edit does not progress cleanly from freshness to craft to payoff; it circles the same action language instead of escalating.","fix":"Restructure into a clear arc: slice hook, freshness detail, one craft beat, one premium plating beat, hero finish."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":12.5,"problem":"The CTA sits too long on screen, making the ending feel static rather than premium and decisive.","fix":"Shorten the CTA hold and reduce text duration so the final beat feels punchier and more commercial."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Brand","timestamp_seconds":7.5,"problem":"The reel lacks a distinct premium brand lock-up moment; it relies almost entirely on process imagery.","fix":"Use the cleanest hero platter shot earlier and reserve the final seconds for an unmistakable brand/visit lock-up."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Audio","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The render does not visibly communicate a finished audio design; SFX and musical dynamics are not evident in the frames and the cut feels flatter than planned.","fix":"If those elements exist in the timeline, make the visual cuts and text beats clearly support them; otherwise simplify to a more confident, cleaner sound bed with fewer editorial tricks."}]
